  "title": "Builder-family detection and diff-aware review posting",
  "summary": "This change makes two parts of the review pipeline stricter and safer. Builder-family detection now reads every word of a `Code-Generator:` trailer (vendor names and model ids alike), refuses to guess when words disagree, and fails the whole run closed when any non-merge commit has no trailer — no reviewer counts, and the reason quotes the offending trailer. Separately, review posting now fetches the pull request's diff and only anchors inline comments on lines the diff actually shows; findings outside it go into the review body with their place named, and findings that do not fit are counted rather than refused.",
  "lenses": [
    "architecture",
    "data-flow"
  ],
